    "description": "**Context**\nOn a brand-new (untouched) sign-up, attribution details aren't shown in the record header — they only appear once a rep has interacted with the record, and otherwise sit off to the right-hand side. Emily wants attribution pulled into the standard header for every status so reps get a consistent, quick view regardless of where the sign-up is in its lifecycle.\n\n**Requirements**\n\n* Move attribution details (source/click info) into the standard record header.\n* Apply across all sign-up statuses, not just conditionally for \"New\" — no differentiator based on status.\n* Exception: the recent click timestamp field does not need to move into the header (per Joyce).\n\n**Constraints / Dependencies**\nNone called out on the call.\n\n**Source**\nFathom — WagerTech <> Jumpr Weekly Sync, 09/23/2026 (https://fathom.video/calls/831090060) — Emily Vandenberg \\~15:05, Joyce Kiddell \\~16:08. Also Taryn's handwritten notes, \"WT Sync 09/23,\" Sign-ups > \"Attribution section moved to header.\"",
